WEBVTT

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.830
Simply wonderful!

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.750
He's still immature, but he has a rare talent!

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.340
He has a bright future ahead!

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.590
Wonderful! Wonderful! Wonderful...

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.220
This is junk. This picture is, too.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.480
And so am I...

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.920
Congratulations, Eruna! Yahoo!

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.380
Yo, yo! Congrats, Eruna!

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.220
You made it past round two!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.550
We'll have a funky pep rally tonight!

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.550
How about you and me? Let's do it!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.890
Congrats, congrats, Eruna!

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.100
I'm sure you can win round three, too!

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.230
- Yo! Yo! Awesome! Hey, hey! Thank you!
- Jeez! I get it already, so will you please stop with that lame rapping?

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.570
I'm glad you like the song
I wrote for you as a present, Eruna!

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.240
I <i>don't</i> like it.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.860
But this isn't your only present.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.070
Hm?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.080
Everyone, are you ready?

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.960
We'll go together on "go," okay?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.290
I want to say the "ready, go" signal!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.380
Is that okay? Is it?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.670
I want to say it, as well.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.920
I've never been entrusted
with that before, so I'm interested.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.430
Minatogawa, if we go after you say it
so calmly, we won't be very energetic.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.430
You should leave this to me!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.140
Everyone, if we talk too loudly,
we'll be found out!

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.640
- I already know you're there.
- But I was supposed to give the signal.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.640
- And it's pretty obvious who's there, too, ryui.
- I said, leave it to me!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.520
- And it's pretty obvious who's there, too, ryui.
- But I—

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.600
I want to do it!

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.270
Didn't we already decide?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.110
- No! No!
- Please ignore us.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.940
I can't do that!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.530
Ah, jeez, I'll give the signal!

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.200
Ready... go!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.280
Congratulations, Eruna!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.700
- Happy birthday, Eruna!
- Ichinomiya, congrats!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.000
Ah, jeez, I can't make out what you're saying!

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.000
Ichinomiya, I came too!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.750
Is it weird that I'm here even though I lost?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.840
No, it's not weird!

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.340
We've gotta have fun during the
club battles! Whether we win or lose—

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.640
Ichinomiya?

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.810
Oh, it's nothing!

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.270
Ichinomiya.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.440
If you're worried about Usamaru, don't be.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.900
Tonkyun was eager about avenging him, too.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:14.480
Huh?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.820
Didn't you hear?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:21.990
Tonkyun will have a match with that
Azumi Sagara after he wins two more times.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.160
Is that right?

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.660
Besides, there are winners and losers
among the other first years, too.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.880
But we've got an upperclassman
that will take good care of them.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.880
"An upperclassman that will
take good care of them"?

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:39.300
Nyamirin!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.840
You all tried hard, didn't you?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.350
I'm gonna go to the drama club's pep rally...

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.980
Are you planning to ditch
your own pep rally, ryui?

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.440
Please turn a blind eye, Bimii.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.610
Nyamirin's bouncy-bouncies are waiting for me!

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.440
Now, we'll start Eruna's pep rally! Cheers!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.400
Cheers!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.250
That was really fun! It was the best present!

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.830
I'm glad you liked it.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.590
I did ask Seisa, but she said
this was past her bedtime.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.840
This is why I don't like club battles...

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.050
I see.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:30.230
Kuzuryu asked who was coming
and then said he'd ruin the mood if he came.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.560
Enoyan shouldn't worry about stuff like that.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.730
The mood is already ruined with you here.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.650
Eruna, you should worry about that more!

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.860
Please worry more about how your
words and actions are hurting me!

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:47.620
Hey, how was the rookie battle
when you were a first year, Shigure?

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.540
Don't tell me you won.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:55.580
I didn't attend Mikagura Academy
yet when I was a first year.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.840
Oh, really?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.340
There's a sister school to Mikagura
Academy that's also like its rival.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.880
I transferred here from that school.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.680
So did Kuzuryu.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:06.890
Huh?

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.180
The sister school that's far west of here

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:17.650
only has sports clubs, in contrast to
Mikagura having only cultural clubs.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.770
They're almost complete opposites.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.990
I enrolled, ready to throw myself
into kendo, my obsession at the time,

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.330
but I couldn't get used to how
everything was win-or-lose there...

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.130
I met Kuzuryu during that time.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.300
A ringer? So you're not a
member of the judo club?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.390
I've got baseball tomorrow,
and track and field the day after.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.520
With your abilities, you'd be able
to do well in any club you join, though.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.440
It looks like I shouldn't bother
with the kendo club, though,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.520
because you're there, Hero Time.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:08.780
Kuzuryu wasn't a member of a single club,
but helped out with different clubs as a ringer.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.200
But...

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:18.210
As his reputation spread, people became
jealous and animosity toward him grew.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:28.220
And then, he accidentally overheard a trusted
friend talking about him behind his back.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:37.230
After that, he couldn't trust
the people around him anymore.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.730
Kuzuryu...!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:46.030
Hero Time, you're the same
as the others, aren't you?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:46.860
Huh?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.200
You can't stand me either, can you?

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.410
Th—

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.710
That was the last time I saw him at that school.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:03.880
Enoyan... You went through all that...?

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.890
And then, in the end, I couldn't
adjust to that school, either,

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.930
so I transferred to Mikagura Academy
right after winning the rookie battle.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:22.190
That's when I found out that
Kuzuryu had also come here.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:28.490
But now, even if we exchange words,
we aren't as friendly as we were back then.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:32.410
You and Enoyan both did the right thing
by coming to Mikagura Academy!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.330
I think it was totally the right thing to do!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:40.790
Anyway, I won my rookie
battle at our sister school.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.300
I almost lost a bunch of times and barely won,

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.920
but I wonder what would've happened
if Kuzuryu had participated, too.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.680
But if you were in the kendo club before,

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.640
why did you choose the manga
research club after coming to Mikagura?

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:57.140
And why did Enoyan choose the art club...?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:02.480
Um... It's a long story,
so let's save it for later.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.150
Tension max! Go!

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.410
Winner, Eruna Ichinomiya.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.530
Go...!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.990
Winner, Eruna Ichinomiya.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.540
Things are going great!

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.330
You've gotten past the fourth round, ryui.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.170
If you win your next match,
you'll be in the quarterfinals, ryui...

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.380
Huh?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.800
Enoyan! Your cute
underclassman has come to visit!

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.010
Hello?

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:41.520
You are completely surrounded! You're making
your mother back in the country cry, too!

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:43.390
Surrender quietly!

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.690
Enoyan! I got some nice, cold milk for y—

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.450
Where's the milk?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.620
Um, uh... I'll go buy it right now! Tee-hee!

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:59.700
It's fine. You don't have to go and buy any.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.170
So this is your stronghold, Enoyan?

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.170
Don't make it sound like a bad place. Here.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:13.800
Oh, I can drink this!

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.590
Did you get this just for me?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.180
'Course not, idiot.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.060
Wow, there are so many
certificates and trophies!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.940
"Innocence"...?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.980
This says "Grand Prize"!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.520
That's amazing!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.730
No, that's not.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.650
No, that <i>is</i>!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.860
That person named "Innocence" is!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.700
That's not a person's name!
It's the title of a painting!

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.790
I wanna see "Innocence."

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.370
Where is it?

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.120
Who knows?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.750
Why won't you show it to me...?

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:59.720
Just kidding. Put that junk away.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.970
Junk?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:06.230
The guy who came up with a naïve title like
"Innocence" without a trace of embarrassment

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:08.730
isn't here anymore.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.150
Huh? Oh! "By Kyoma Kuzuryu"!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.990
Well, did you need something?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:18.910
Um, well, it's not that I <i>needed</i> anything...

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:19.740
Huh?

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.950
But I just came up with something!
A favor I wanna ask you!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:23.750
I refuse.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.460
I didn't say what it was yet!

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:30.250
Enoyan!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.000
Huh?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.750
Please draw me!

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:36.920
I want you to draw how you see me!

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.800
And if necessary...

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:41.680
H-Hey!

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:44.270
...I'll take it all off!

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.060
Even if you turn me down,
I'll come back tomorrow!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.940
Don't worry, I'll turn you down tomorrow, too.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.650
Oh, is this the time?

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:56.610
Please make sure you
watch my next match, okay?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:58.610
Why should I?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.160
Because I want you to, Enoyan!

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.490
I will if I feel like it.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.120
It's a promise!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.460
What was that about?
I have no idea what she's thinking, as usual.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.140
Ichinomiya, over here! Over here!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.350
That's...

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:37.110
She likes high places as usual, huh...

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.500
Why... is he riding a panda?

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.380
At least he should have gone with a pig.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.720
Is my opponent today another
supporting character from the drama club?

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.350
And a pig at that, after that rabbit?

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:07.890
Maybe I'll roast you whole and eat you up!

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.900
It's true that I'm a supporting
character from the drama club.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:18.280
But us supporting characters
have our own ways of fighting.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.280
Begin the match.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.200
I'll make mincemeat out of you in a second.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:26.870
Molto Accento!

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:41.470
I get it! She can't increase the
gravity of a wide space all at once!

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.640
If he approaches her like that without
letting her narrow down her target—

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:54.980
You're just third-rate,
with the shallow thinking of a pig.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:59.730
Do you think a super first-rate performer like
me wouldn't be able to see through that plan?

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.200
You can boast all you want.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.740
If you think you can beat me, go ahead and try.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:10.750
Or are you too scared
to come near a moving pig?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.080
You swine...!

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:19.000
Don't talk like that to a noble human!

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.840
One piggy! Two piggies!

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:26.430
Look, look, Piggy! They're all gonna die!

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.850
Last one! Three pi—

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.600
I've caught you, Miss Third-Rate Performer.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:42.150
So what? How are you going to
break my crystals in that state?

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.490
All you can do is wait until time runs out.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:48.410
Aren't you the one in trouble
because you're running out of time?

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:49.620
Wh—?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.080
The end is in sight.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.630
It looks like your performance is over.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.880
Don't tell me... you were
aiming for this from the start?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.390
I discovered after watching
your match with Usamaru yesterday

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.600
that your ability cannot be used continuously.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:17.190
After you perform for a certain amount
of time, you appear to require a rest.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.980
And then, there is a time lag before you
can activate your ability again, isn't there?

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:25.150
In yesterday's match,
after your performance ended,

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.030
all you did was stand
on top of the pipe organ.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.160
Once your ability has stopped and
you cannot float in the air anymore,

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.620
all you can do is hide it like that.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.250
But that was the right thing to do.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.460
If you fought fair and square,

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.880
you would not have
been able to beat Usamaru.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.960
Shut up, you lowly pig!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.590
You will be defeated by a supporting character.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:50.890
Ad Lib Role!

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.610
Winner, Tonkyun.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.400
Tonkyun, you did it!

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.450
What're those?

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.700
Bunny ears!

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:12.450
That's too passionate! I think I'm gonna cry!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.370
Aren't you excited, Ichinomiya?

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:15.290
Huh?

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:16.620
You haven't realized?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:21.880
Next is the fifth round, when the match
between you and Tonkyun will be a reality!

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.340
Huh? What?!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.100
The match is about to start, ryui!

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:39.350
Whoever wins here will be
in the quarterfinals, ryui!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.150
Are you two ready, ryui?

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.110
I won't lose, Tonkyun.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.860
There's a reason why I must win.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:52.370
I don't plan on losing, either.
For the drama club—

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.870
...and for myself.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:10.590
"Taking applications for club members now.
Beautiful girls welcome.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.890
Beautiful girls may rise
immediately to management positions...

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.470
Lolis will receive a snack allowance.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.430
Interested girls should contact
first-year Eruna Ichinomiya."

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:23.150
Don't tell me that's what
that kid wanted to show me...

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.940
Eruna! I did say that the rookie
battle would help promote your club,

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:27.940
but that's not what I meant, ryui!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.110
Besides, your descriptions of the types of
members you want are too sketchy, ryui!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:35.950
What's wrong? I even had Katai
write it all cute for me, too!

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:37.950
Begin the match.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.870
Before he activates his power, I'll get one!

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.340
I thought you'd do that.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.550
Even so—

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.760
Now! Sudden tension max!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.510
Go!

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.470
Shall we heat things up?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:01.980
Ad Lib Role!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.520
Oh, no!

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.230
If I'm this far away...

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:17.740
How ironic... The bullet is obviously
slower than the person who fired it.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.160
Which is why...

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.700
...I can see it, almost too well.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.540
No way!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.290
Even if I'm the one who wins,

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:32.170
it won't change the fact that a member
of the After-School Six is moving up.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.300
Please cheer from the stands next time.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.680
I told you, didn't I?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.520
That there's a reason why I must win!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.520
This is the first time I'm
showing this to anyone.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:55.990
I was naïvely thinking to save it
until my match with Asuhi.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.580
That was a wonderful secret weapon.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.210
However, you have one blade,
while I have two.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.880
I will challenge you with
twice the swordsmanship.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.590
Please do not think badly of me.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:21.010
It's fine. For some reason,
I don't feel like I can lose right now!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:26.060
I feel like I've got a different kind
of blood flowing through my body!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.800
Shall I deal the final blow now?

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:59.140
I will show you that light can be
burnt to nothing with flames!

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.770
Her speed is increasing as she fights...

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.850
Is she improving?

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.150
But I have two swords...

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:17.240
That's right. But Tonkyun,
this isn't just a sword of light—

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.280
It's a bayonet!

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:20.490
Don't tell me...

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.540
Winner, Eruna Ichinomiya.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.750
Well done.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:37.460
For the next match, I will be
the one to cheer from the stands.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:51.770
You lost?

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:58.110
In the quarterfinal after that, Haruka Toishi
from the broadcast club beat me easily...

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.740
Your abilities were completely analyzed,

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.570
and there was the difference
in your real strengths, too, ryui.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.370
What the heck?

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:08.160
And I was gonna give this to you
as a present when you won, too.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:08.660
Huh?

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:12.580
Didn't you ask me to draw a picture of you?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.210
Then, could this be...

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.800
...me?!

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.130
I call it, "Innocent Full Throttle"!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.220
Now that I think about it, you said you wanted
to see "Innocent Unlabeled," too, right?

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.180
Where did I put that again...?

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.810
It's fine. I think I can
imagine what it looks like...

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:32.230
Thanks to you, I've got my touch back.

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:36.110
If you want, I'll draw you
another one—no, as many as you like!

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:37.900
No, thanks!

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.780
Eruna, hurry, ryui!

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.900
The finals are about to start, ryui!

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:54.420
Why...?

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:56.920
Asuhi...

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.920
...lost?

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:05.260
Winner, Otone Fujishiro.

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:43.570
Enoyan, that picture you drew was lovely!

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:47.910
It's because I drink milk every day.
You should drink it too. It's fresh.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.370
Fresh? You mean, you personally
milk a cow every morning?!

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:53.160
I'll leave that to your imagination.

00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:57.040
Give me a minute. I'm going to imagine it.

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:02.500
You're milking. Milking!
Enoyan is milking furiously!

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:07.630
Whoa! There's the underhand grip!
How unexpected!

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.260
How'd your imagination go <i>there</i>?

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:09.890
Oh!

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:10.760
What's wrong?

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:12.850
Seisa is looking this way!

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:15.060
I guess she wants to do a preview too?

00:24:15.270 --> 00:24:18.020
No, I don't really want to do one.

00:24:18.230 --> 00:24:22.020
A preview together with Seisa!
A trailer for our happy wedding!

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:23.770
Like an opening prelude!

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:25.280
I don't know what you mean.

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:28.490
Then do a preview you understand!
Please show me how it's done!

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:30.200
I will learn from it!

00:24:30.410 --> 00:24:32.450
If you insist...

00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:35.080
Next time, "Izayoi Seeing."

00:24:35.290 --> 00:24:39.080
Maybe something wonderful
will happen beneath the star-filled sky.

00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:42.210
Izayoi! Oh, so that's not read
literally as "sixteen nights"!

00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:45.170
Way to go, Seisa! I learned something!

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.630
Seriously...?
